    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your intellect shapes your magic as much as your charisma.</p><ul data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"1117\"><li data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"825\"><p data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"825\">You gain proficiency in <strong data-start=\"646\" data-end=\"656\">Arcana</strong> and in <strong data-start=\"664\" data-end=\"691\">calligrapher’s supplies</strong> or <strong data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"714\">jeweler’s tools</strong> (your choice). If you are already proficient in Arcana, your proficiency bonus is doubled for Arcana checks.</p></li><li data-start=\"826\" data-end=\"1117\"><p data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"1117\">When you make an <strong data-start=\"845\" data-end=\"890\">Arcana, History, Investigation, or Nature</strong> check, you can use your <strong data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"936\">Charisma modifier</strong> in place of the ability modifier normally used. You can do this a number of times equal to your <strong data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1058\">Intelligence modifier</strong> per long rest, or by expending a Bardic Inspiration die.</p></li><li data-start=\"826\" data-end=\"1117\"><p>When a creature benefitting from one of your <strong>Prototype Imbuements</strong> expends a bardic inspiration dice, it adds your Intelligence Modifier to the roll if it is an Attack Roll or Ability Check.</p></li><li data-start=\"826\" data-end=\"1117\"><p>Your Bardic Inspiration on a creature bearing one of your imbuments does not expire until the imbument does or it is used. You cannot regain this use of bardic inspiration while it is not expired.</p></li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
